  "summary": "A jacketed vessel has an outer jacket around the lower part of the vessel. A heating or cooling medium (steam, hot oil, chilled water) flows through the jacket space and heats or cools the contents through the vessel wall without mixing with them. A spiral baffle guides the medium for better heat transfer.",
